---
import SectionTitle from "../layouts/SectionTitle.astro";
import PortfolioNav from "../layouts/PortfolioNav.astro";
import VideoScript from "../layouts/VideoScript.astro";
import Video from "../layouts/Video.astro";
import Image from "../layouts/Image.astro";
import Footer from "../layouts/Footer.astro";

---

<html lang="en">
    <body class="inventory bg-[#17212b] min-h-screen text-[#d5e1e8]">
        <PortfolioNav />
        <SectionTitle
            title="Inventory System"
            imgsrc="/portfolio/inventory.png"
            titlecolor="text-[#67c5d8]"
        />
        <main class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 space-y-3 mb-6">
            <h2>Overview</h2>
            <p>
                I developed an interface system, inspired by the Resident Evil
                series of games, which allows the player to sort and perform
                actions on items they have collected. Furthermore, this system
                introduces a weight constraint that affects the player's
                movements.
            </p>

            <h2>Used Tools</h2>
            <p>
                I used Unreal Engine 6 in blueprint to create this system and
                the Common UI plugin to design the interfaces.
            </p>

            <h2>How It Works</h2>
            <p>
                Items are displayed in the grid according to an image assigned
                to them and a size based on grid squares. The larger the items,
                the more space they take up in this grid.
            </p>
            <Image imgsrc="/portfolio/presentation.png" />
            <p>
                Each of these items contains information that can be viewed,
                following a dedicated structure, within this inventory, such as
                rarity and utility.
            </p>
            <Image imgsrc="/portfolio/infosobjets.png" />

            <p>
                The player can also perform actions on these items via a context
                menu, such as using them, discarding a single item or the entire
                stack of items from the inventory.
            </p>
            <Image imgsrc="/portfolio/actions.png" />
            <p>
                To increase the available space, the player can interact with
                bags found in the environment to gain extra space by placing
                them around the existing inventory.
            </p>
            <Video videosrc="/portfolio/addspace.mp4" />
            <p>
                Each item has a weight that affects the maximum weight the
                player can carry. When a weight threshold is reached, the
                player's speed will decrease.
            </p>
            <Video videosrc="/portfolio/weight.mp4" />

            <h2>Links</h2>
            <p>
                <span class="bold">Project repository</span>: <a
                    href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/12dPcvhTwP5UI-ABs5rqb8YJtVe_nktw6/view?usp=sharing"
                    >https://drive.google.com/file/d/12dPcvhTwP5UI-ABs5rqb8YJtVe_nktw6/view?usp=sharing</a
                >
            </p>
